  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "Dealing with credit card debt can be overwhelming, but there are several steps you can take to manage and reduce your debt. Here are some tips for negotiating with creditors:\n\n1. Create a budget: Start by creating a detailed budget that outlines your income and expenses. This will help you identify areas where you can cut back and free up more money to pay off your debt.\n\n2. Contact your creditors: Reach out to your creditors and explain your situation. Be honest and transparent about your debt and your ability to pay. Ask for a lower interest rate or a payment plan that works for you.\n\n3. Consider a debt consolidation loan: A debt consolidation loan can help you pay off multiple credit card debts with a single loan. This can reduce your interest rate and make it easier to manage your debt.\n\n4. Look for credit counseling services: Credit counseling services can help you develop a plan to pay off your debt and avoid defaulting on your credit cards. They can also provide you with guidance on how to improve your credit score.\n\n5. Consider bankruptcy: If you are unable to pay off your debt, bankruptcy may be an option. However, it is a serious decision that can have long-term consequences, so be sure to consult with a bankruptcy attorney before making a decision.\n\nRemember, it's important to communicate with your creditors and seek professional advice to develop a plan that works for you.",
